<Page title="Open source. Accountable engineering." description="ArtemisKit is an open-source AI assurance toolkit by Vorbtech Innovative Solutions, founded by Babangida Tsowa. It helps builders examine model responses, tool-using agents and operational behaviour through explicit scenarios and inspectable evidence. The project supports better technical decisions while keeping limitations and human judgment visible." eyebrow="An open-source project by VIS"><h2>Why this project exists</h2><p>A convincing demo can hide a fragile workflow. Teams need a practical way to ask specific questions: did the task complete, were the rules respected, and what evidence supports the answer?</p><p>ArtemisKit turns those questions into reviewable tests. Its open-source foundation makes the mechanics available for inspection, independent use and contribution.</p><h2>How does ArtemisKit relate to VIS?</h2><p>ArtemisKit has its own developer identity and community. Vorbtech Innovative Solutions is the organisation behind the project and offers separately scoped implementation and AI Assurance services. You can use the toolkit independently of those services.</p><h2>Who is it for?</h2><p>Developers, evaluators, researchers, security teams and technical reviewers working on AI systems. Governance stakeholders can use scoped findings to inform review, with the assistance of relevant technical and domain owners.</p><h2>What do we stand for?</h2><ul><li><strong>Inspectability:</strong> Keep requirements, methods and evidence understandable.</li><li><strong>Scope:</strong> Test a defined question and state what remains unknown.</li><li><strong>Human responsibility:</strong> Keep consequential decisions with authorised people.</li><li><strong>Useful participation:</strong> Welcome better scenarios, documentation, code and challenge.</li></ul><p><a href="https://www.vorbtech.com.ng/">Visit Vorbtech Innovative Solutions</a> or <a href="/community/">contribute to ArtemisKit</a>.</p></Page>
